        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "57665220-2b48-5abd-8011-e7cd179a2a7c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Toy Story, Toy Story 2\n- Companies: Pixar Animation Studios, Walt Disney Pictures\n- People: Stylianos Kyriakides, Annie Potts\n- Roles: Bo Peep\n- Events: Boston Marathon, Second World War\n- Places: Paphos, Cyprus, Greece\n\nFacts:\n- Toy Story is a 1995 American computer-animated buddy comedy adventure film produced by Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures.\n- In 1946, Stylianos Kyriakides won the Boston Marathon to raise money for Greeks facing severe poverty after the Second World War.\n- Stylianos Kyriakides was born on January 15, 1910, in Paphos, Cyprus, and died in December 1987.\n- In the 1990s, Annie Potts voiced Bo Peep in the animated films Toy Story (1995) and Toy Story 2 (1999).",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5523a571-4e71-57a3-8ccd-6e53160655aa",
        "text": "Page: Toy Story. Sentence: Toy Story is a 1995 American computer-animated buddy comedy adventure film produced by Pixar Animation Studios for Walt Disney Pictures.\nPage: Stylianos Kyriakides. Sentence: Stylianos \"Stelios\" Kyriakides (Greek: Στυλιανός \"Στέλιος\" Κυριακίδης ; January 15, 1910 (Paphos, Cyprus OS/NS) – December 1987) was a marathon runner who came first at the Boston Marathon in 1946, with the aim of raising money to provide food and shelter to the Greeks, who were experiencing severe poverty issues from the Second World War.\nPage: Annie Potts. Sentence: In the 1990s, she voiced Bo Peep in the animated films \"Toy Story\" (1995) and \"Toy Story 2\" (1999).",
